  "notes": "Herdr fork preview (wwelder/herdr): an agent can wake the owner\n\nSource: ede64479417864532685fb2ec80d790413cd6e57.\n\n- `herdr gram send --critical \"<text>\"` (API: `gram.send` with `critical: true`) pushes the gram to the owner's devices as an iOS critical alert, which plays through silent mode and Focus. It is for emergencies only. Guests never get a critical gram, not even as an ordinary alert.\n- HerdrUp shows it as time-sensitive until Apple grants its critical-alerts entitlement and the owner allows critical alerts.\n\nThe Linux and Windows assets were built by the manual Build artifacts workflow. GitHub's macOS arm64 runners had no capacity, so both macOS assets were built on an Apple Silicon Mac from a clean checkout of the same commit with the workflow's settings (Rust 1.96.1, Zig 0.16.0, libghostty ReleaseSafe, SIMD off).\n\nUpdate with `herdr update` on the preview channel.",
